NAME
    erase - zero a disk's leading sectors

SYNOPSIS
    erase disk

DESCRIPTION
    Destructive. Zeroes the disk's first sectors (partition table plus early
    filesystem metadata) so it can be freshly partitioned. Requires the literal
    word "disk". Refused while a filesystem is mounted. A builtin (it must run
    when nothing is mounted).

SEE ALSO
    partition, format, unmount
